# Sibling to .gitignore for `fd`-driven scans (e.g. lint walkers). Excludes
# verbatim third-party content we never want linted as natural language.
#
# This is the load-bearing one for prose lint: auto-textlint discovers files with
# `fd --extension md --extension txt`, so the corpus is only spared here —
# .textlintignore alone would not stop it, since the paths arrive as explicit
# arguments. A licence derives its force from being byte-identical to the
# published text, so an autofixable rule (apostrophes, terminology) rewriting it
# would do real damage.
internal/bridge/license/spdx/
